  "name": "atx-v1_1/behavioral-profile-extra-member",
  "description": "An ATX v1.1 credential signed with the baseline behavioralProfile (checksum, generatedAt, observationDays), carrying a fourth member in it, riskLevel \"low\", written AFTER signing. The credential schema of atx-spec §1.1 gives behavioralProfile exactly those three members (additionalProperties false), and JCS(TBS) holds the profile as those three members (§1.3a.2), so no signature covers a profile with a fourth. The verifier MUST REJECT with a signature-validation reason. A verifier that decodes the profile into its three fields drops the fourth member, projects the signed profile and wrongly ACCEPTs a credential carrying a member its signature does not cover.",
  "requirement": "§1.1: the credential schema gives behavioralProfile exactly checksum, generatedAt and observationDays, so a fourth member added after signing leaves a profile the TBS has no value for, a signature failure",
